1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,400
Most leaders that I speak to feel the same tension. The AI space feels chaotic. Every week there is a

2
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:11,600
new model, a new startup, or a new headline claiming some kind of a breakthrough, and it's

3
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:17,200
very difficult to tell what actually matters for your work and what is just noise. So let's talk

4
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:22,800
about what you actually should know about the AI landscape. So first of all, you hear many names

5
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:28,560
in the market, but for practical day-to-day knowledge work, four ecosystems really dominate.

6
00:00:28,560 --> 00:00:34,880
You have Chet-GPT from OpenAI, Gemini from Google, Co-Pilot from Microsoft, and then Claude from

7
00:00:34,880 --> 00:00:40,560
Anthropic. Some others that you may see include DeepSeek, which shocked the market with a high

8
00:00:40,560 --> 00:00:47,200
performing low-cost model released last year, Grok from X with access to real-time social data,

9
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:54,640
or Meta's Open Llama models. Innovation is really happening everywhere, but if your goal is

10
00:00:54,640 --> 00:00:59,120
implementing within teams and organizations, you should really just focus first on the platforms

11
00:00:59,120 --> 00:01:04,400
that integrate with major productivity suites, offer enterprise governance, and consistently

12
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:10,480
ship new capabilities, which again today primarily means Chet-GPT, Gemini, Co-Pilot, and Claude.

13
00:01:11,200 --> 00:01:16,080
But let's zoom out as well. If we look at the last three years, the evolution is very clear.

14
00:01:16,720 --> 00:01:22,560
In 2022-23, when AI was just launched, it functioned primarily as a chat-based assistant.

15
00:01:22,560 --> 00:01:27,120
So you would type a prompt, it would generate a response, and it really felt like a capable

16
00:01:27,120 --> 00:01:33,600
but very junior co-worker waiting for your instructions. In 2024, the interaction expanded

17
00:01:33,600 --> 00:01:39,680
beyond text, so multimodal capabilities meant that AI could analyze documents, interpret images,

18
00:01:39,680 --> 00:01:43,520
process voice, and in some cases even understand what's happening on your screen.

19
00:01:44,160 --> 00:01:51,920
In 2025, the shift became structural. AI started moving beyond individual prompts and into recurring

20
00:01:51,920 --> 00:01:58,640
workflows. Instead of asking AI to help with one task at a time, people could increasingly give it

21
00:01:58,640 --> 00:02:05,360
persistent instructions, connect it to relevant context and tools, and build repeatable ways of

22
00:02:05,360 --> 00:02:10,880
working around it. AI was becoming less something you occasionally consulted and more something

23
00:02:10,880 --> 00:02:19,040
built into how you work. And in 2026, we've moved another step forward. AI can increasingly carry

24
00:02:19,040 --> 00:02:26,640
work forward for you. This is where agentic AI becomes important. Agentic systems can take a goal,

25
00:02:26,640 --> 00:02:32,320
work through multiple steps, use tools and connected information, take actions, observe

26
00:02:32,320 --> 00:02:37,920
what happened, and decide what to do next without requiring you to direct every individual step.

27
00:02:38,720 --> 00:02:44,720
That does not mean fully autonomous digital employees have arrived. The most useful systems

28
00:02:44,800 --> 00:02:49,920
today still work with bounded autonomy. Humans decide what AI can access,

29
00:02:49,920 --> 00:02:55,280
what it is allowed to do, where approval is required, and where judgment and accountability

30
00:02:55,280 --> 00:03:01,680
must stay with us. So the progression is becoming clear. AI started by answering us,

31
00:03:01,680 --> 00:03:07,360
then became capable of working with more kinds of information, then became built into our recurring

32
00:03:07,360 --> 00:03:12,400
workflows, and now it can increasingly carry parts of those workflows forward for us.

33
00:03:13,280 --> 00:03:17,600
And that changes the question we should be asking. It is no longer only,

34
00:03:17,600 --> 00:03:23,040
what can I ask AI to help me with? Increasingly, it is, given what AI can now do,

35
00:03:23,040 --> 00:03:27,760
how should this work happen in the first place? And what should the human and AI each be responsible

36
00:03:27,760 --> 00:03:31,120
for?

